<title>UK: TI seen higher after top-end results.</title>
<headline>TI seen higher after top-end results.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in TI Group were expected to open higher on Thursday after the company revealed results at the top end of analysts expectations.</p>
<p>&quot;They were a very good set of results and I think the market will be very pleased with them,&quot; said Robert Speed, engineering analyst at Henderson Crosthwaite.</p>
<p>Half-year pretax profit of 112.1 million stg excluding exceptional items was down from 125 million stg the year before but topped average forecasts around 110 million stg.</p>
<p>The shares closed at 569p on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027</p>
